    "country_code": null,
    "payload": {
      "item_type": "disturbance",
      "source": "jtwc_abio",
      "source_key": "jtwc_abio|north_indian_ocean_area|invest_91b",
      "content_hash": "c6e70b55b27be28e",
      "platform_summary": "10.3N 88.7E | winds 23-28 kt | 1005 mb | HIGH",
      "platform_location": "10.3N 88.7E",
      "wind": "23-28 kt",
      "risk_48h": null,
      "risk_7d": null,
      "next_update": null,
      "raw_text": "(1) THE AREA OF CONVECTION (INVEST 91B) PREVIOUSLY LOCATED NEAR \n9.5N 93.2E IS NOW LOCATED NEAR 10.3N 88.7E, APPROXIMATELY 250 NM \nSOUTH-SOUTHWEST OF PORT BLAIR. ANIMATED ENHANCED INFRARED IMAGERY \n(MSI) AND A 311200Z SSMIS F-17 91GHZ MICROWAVE IMAGE DEPICT AN \nELONGATED LLCC WITH DEEP, PERSISTENT CONVECTION WITH CURVED CONVECTIVE \nBANDING AND FORMATIVE RAIN BANDS IN THE NORTHERN QUADRANT. A 311437Z \nMETOP-B ASCAT PASS REVEALED 20 KTS WRAPPING AROUND THE ELONGATED LLCC, \nWHILE A SMALL REGION OF 25 KT WINDS IS PRESENT IN THE EASTERN FLANK. \nENVIRONMENTAL ANALYSIS REVEALS A FAVORABLE ENVIRONMENT FOR DEVELOPMENT \nWITH LOW TO MODERATE EASTERLY VERTICAL WIND SHEAR (VWS) OF 10-15KTS, \nGOOD UPPER-LEVEL WESTWARD AND POLEWARD OUTFLOW, AND WARM SEA SURFACE \nTEMPERATURES (SST) OF 29-30C. GLOBAL DETERMINISTIC AND ENSEMBLE MODELS \nARE WITHIN MODERATE TO HIGH AGREEMENT ON THE FUTURE EVOLUTION OF 91B, \nWITH AI-BASED MODELS SHOWING THE QUICKEST DEVELOPMENT INTO A TROPICAL \nCYCLONE WITHIN 6 TO 12 HOURS, WHILE PHYSICS-BASED MODELS DEPICT A \nSLOWER INTENSIFICATION AND DEVELOPMENT AFTER 24 HOURS. ALL MODELS ARE \nIN AGREEMENT IN 91B TRACKING NORTHWESTWARD TOWARD MAINLAND INDIA OVER \nTHE NEXT 24-48HRS. MAXIMUM SUSTAINED SURFACE WINDS ARE ESTIMATED AT 23 \nTO 28 KNOTS. MINIMUM SEA LEVEL PRESSURE IS ESTIMATED TO BE NEAR 1005 \nMB. THE POTENTIAL FOR THE DEVELOPMENT OF A SIGNIFICANT TROPICAL \nCYCLONE WITHIN THE NEXT 24 HOURS REMAINS HIGH. SEE REF A (WTIO21 PGTW \n310600) FOR FURTHER DETAILS.",
      "metadata": {
        "basin_section": "NORTH INDIAN OCEAN AREA (MALAY PENINSULA WEST TO COAST OF AFRICA)",
